A_592 - When you buy bread it is usual to store it in a paper bag, often inside some cabinet. If you place the paper bag in an airtight sealable plastic bag (like those sometimes used to store certain products in the freezer), then the bread should not dry out because the moisture does not escape and it should stay soft for longer . In addition to this, if the plastic bag were transparent and the bread was left in a non-dark place, perhaps at that point the preservation would be further improved. If a quartz crystal were left nearby, that should also have positive effects.